		<title type="html"><![CDATA[PhysBAM released as open source]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=22582#p22582"><![CDATA[
I just noticed that several parts of the PhysBAM library are open source and for public download now: <a href="http://physbam.stanford.edu/" class="postlink">http://physbam.stanford.edu/</a><br><br>PhysBAM_Tools, PhysBAM_Geometry, PhysBAM_OpenGL and PhysBAM_Ray_Tracing.<br><br>The license seems to be a 2-clause permissive BSD license. The project has been used in movies and lead by Jon Su and Ron Fewkiw from Stanford University.<br><a href="http://physbam.stanford.edu/links/getcode.html" class="postlink">http://physbam.stanford.edu/links/getcode.html</a><br><a href="http://physbam.stanford.edu/links/download.html" class="postlink">http://physbam.stanford.edu/links/download.html</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Wed Mar 16, 2011 10:26 pm</p><hr />
